    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "39 Beaufield Park, Stillorgan, Co. Dublin\r\nExceptional Development Opportunity with Full Planning Permission\r\n\r\nTurley Property Advisors are delighted to present 39 Beaufield Park, Stillorgan, Co. Dublin, an outstanding opportunity to acquire a charming detached home on a substantial south-facing site with the benefit of full planning permission for both a significant extension to the existing residence and the construction of a new dwelling to the side of the property, in place of the existing garage. The approved plans provide for the existing house to be extended while also creating a separate dwelling (39A Beaufield Park), offering exceptional flexibility for homeowners, developers and investors alike. Planning Reference Number: D25A/0096/WEB\r\n\r\nThe existing home extends to approximately 65 sq.m (700 sq.ft.) and is presented in excellent decorative order throughout. The accommodation briefly comprises:\r\n\r\nEntrance hallway\r\nBright living room\r\nModern fully fitted kitchen/dining room\r\nContemporary family bathroom\r\nTwo generous double bedrooms\r\nGarage with electricity\r\n\r\nThe property further benefits from a magnificent south-facing rear garden, providing exceptional outdoor space and enormous potential. To the front there is off-street parking together with a garage, which forms the footprint of the approved new dwelling.\r\n\r\nPlanning permission has been granted for:\r\n\r\nA substantial extension and remodelling of the existing house.\r\nThe construction of a separate detached dwelling (39A Beaufield Park) with its own independent vehicular access.\r\n\r\nWhether you are seeking a family home with future expansion potential, a multi-generational living solution or an exciting development opportunity in one of South Dublin's most sought-after residential locations, this property is certain to appeal.\r\n\r\nFeatures\r\nDetached 2-bedroom residence extending to approx. 65 sq.m.\r\nFull planning permission for a substantial extension to the existing house.\r\nFull planning permission for a separate detached dwelling (39A Beaufield Park).\r\nExceptional south-facing rear garden.\r\nOff-street parking.\r\nGarage with approved redevelopment potential.\r\nQuiet, mature and highly desirable residential estate.\r\nWalking distance to Stillorgan Village and excellent local amenities.\r\nExcellent transport links including the N11, M50, Dublin Bus and LUAS at Sandyford.\r\nOutstanding primary and secondary schools nearby.\r\nBER: F\r\n\r\nLocation\r\n\r\nBeaufield Park is one of Stillorgan's most established and sought-after residential addresses, renowned for its mature surroundings, generous gardens and superb convenience. Situated just minutes from Stillorgan Village, residents enjoy an excellent selection of cafés, restaurants, supermarkets and boutique shopping together with the nearby Stillorgan Shopping Centre.\r\n\r\nThe area is exceptionally well served by both public and private transport. Numerous Dublin Bus routes operate nearby, while the LUAS Green Line at Sandyford and Kilmacud is within easy reach. The N11 and M50 motorway provide swift access to Dublin City Centre, Dublin Airport and the wider national road network.\r\n\r\nThe property is surrounded by an excellent choice of highly regarded schools including St. Laurence's, Oatlands College, Mount Anville, Blackrock College, St. Andrew's College and University College Dublin (UCD). There is also an abundance of recreational amenities close by including Deerpark, Kilmacud Crokes GAA Club, Elm Park Golf Club, Leopardstown Racecourse and the coastal villages of Blackrock and Dún Laoghaire.\r\n\r\nOffering the rare combination of an existing turnkey home, an exceptional south-facing site and valuable planning permission in a prime South Dublin location, 39 Beaufield Park represents a unique opportunity that is seldom brought to the market."
      },
